<title>NETHERLANDS: Van Lanschot cuts DSM EPS '96 estimate.</title>
<headline>Van Lanschot cuts DSM EPS '96 estimate.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of earnings update.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>DSM		 Chemicals     174.50  Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Market performer. DSM's preliminary profit figure clearly disappointing. DSM and analysts surprised by impact of higher naphtha prices, stagnant Q4 plastics prices. But things are improving: naphtha prices now falling while plastic prices are finally rising again. DSM's margins at bottom in Q4, with results further depressed by new polypropylene plant coming on-stream, maintenance stops. Long-term, new plant will improve DSM's cost structure and earnings seen rising in 1997.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS    (previous)    P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	29.65    (n/a)	 5.9     8.00</p>
<p>    1996		   24.25    26.25	 7.2     8.00</p>
<p>    1997		   29.50    (n/a)	 5.9     8.00</p>
<p>    1998		   32.00    (n/a)	 5.5     8.00</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
